zl1 -- the SECOND heat cause (cpufreq governor), first device run, 2026-09-25
==========================================================================

One boot throughout: boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5 (read before the run, after it, and
again after the health check; it did not change). Nothing was flashed, no partition was written, no
block device was opened, no service was restarted, the container was never stopped.

Host: this laptop.  Device: root@10.15.19.82 (rndis0), serial 33e80afe.  THE DEVICE CLOCK IS WRONG
-- it reads 1970-02-13 -- so every timestamp the instrument prints is wrong and the real date is the
one in this header. That is the same defect docs 100 records for journal queries.

The only thing this experiment writes is four cpufreq files. The value it writes back is the fix's
own (`interactive`), and the boot's zl1-cpufreq-governor unit writes it again on the next boot.

