  == the verdict
     window A was the fix installed ('interactive'); B was the cores PINNED ('performance'); C was
     'interactive' again. Busy: A 0.81, B 0.54, C 0.82 of 4 cores (a READING, not a gate: a governor
     changes the clock a core runs at, and this figure counts busy TIME, so the two are not expected
     to track).
     the largest warming from A to B on any tsens zone: 6.8 C  (thermal_zone12 (tsens_tz_sensor11))
     and from A to C (the control, same state as A):   8.4 C  (thermal_zone9 (tsens_tz_sensor8))
     the threshold this experiment calls a cost: 0.2 C -- two steps of the instrument's 0.1 C

     -> CONTAMINATED: B was warmer than A by 6.8 C, but C -- the SAME state as A -- is still 8.4 C
        above A. So the warming did not come back with the governor's state and was not caused by it:
        the phone drifted, or the load did. A statement about this RUN, not about the governor.

        (exit 1)

     The cores read 'interactive' cpu0=interactive cpu1=interactive cpu2=interactive
     cpu3=interactive -- the state it started in.

